{ "RB3_HANDS_ATTACH_PROBE", "off", FlagClass::Probe, FlagRead::Presence, "skinning", "probe: W2.8f (Wave 11) the TRUSTWORTHY rest-capture-free hands instrument. Two palette-INTERNAL invariants on the UPLOADED palette (bones.bones[]) at the DrawMesh dualskin site, NOT gated on wext so it co-samples the full 61-106u smear trajectory. TIER1 (secondary, amplitude): full-palette per-bone rest-coherence sweep with POINTER-IDENTITY freshness validation (repoint bound->own IS a ptr change -> recapture, killing the W2.8e stale-bone confound) reporting angle(off_b*restW_b,I) + pose-indep xcheck angle(inv(off_b),restW_b). TIER2 (PRIMARY, pose-tracking, rest-FREE): parent/child joint-attachment ||j_b*P[parent]-j_b*P[child]|| with j_b=-off_b.v AND exact inverse(off_b).v. FINDING: exact-joint TIER2 reads ~0 (<=0.33u over 2214 hand samples, == clean control) => the hands palette is inter-bone COHERENT (joints attached, matching A.S3 wrist-attached); the visible 106u smear is a mesh-shell/offset conjugation (TIER1 87deg == A.S1) NOT a joint dislocation, so joint-attachment is the WRONG Wave-12 gate. A5 -off.v approximate joint is CONFOUNDED (false-positive 90u on the clean greaserjacket control); the exact inverse(off).v joint is required. Value name-substr/1/*; render-inert, getenv-gated, flag-OFF byte-identical (drawlog 792) [Rnd_Wgpu_RB3.cpp]", "RB3_HANDS_ATTACH_PROBE" },
