{ "RB3_HANDS_PERFRAME_CONJ", "off", FlagClass::Feature, FlagRead::Presence, "skinning", "not-live: W2.8c per-frame pose-aware appendage (hands/fingers) basis correction — the one remaining fix class after the two static approaches (RB3_HANDS_BIND_FIX seed, RB3_HANDS_POSEAWARE rigid wrist-collapse) were empirically killed. Keeps every hand/finger bone bound to its OWN live per-member bone (articulation preserved, anti-rigid-collapse) and each Poll rewrites its palette offset so the live bone's rotation is applied ABOUT the authored magnet frame: offset_b(t)=inv(A_b)*inv(L_b(t0))*L_b(t)*A_b*inv(L_b(t)), cancelling the growing R*sin(theta) twist per bone instead of collapsing the hand rigidly. A_b/L_b(t0) captured once per mesh at latch, only L_b(t) re-sampled per Poll (unlatched apply, no bind re-bake drift). Mutually exclusive with RB3_HANDS_POSEAWARE (only one runs) and with RebindHeadHandsAtRest (skips hand/finger/glove meshes when ON so A_b stays pristine). flag-OFF byte-identical (getenv-cached early return in BandCharacter::NativeConjHandsPerFrame) [BandCharacter.cpp]", "RB3_HANDS_PERFRAME_CONJ" },
{ "RB3_HANDS_POSEAWARE", "off", FlagClass::Feature, FlagRead::Presence, "skinning", "not-live: W2.8 BL-A1 rigid-anchor hands/fingers fix — collapses the pose-varying multi-bone rotation-basis divergence that flings distal finger verts into sheets (the 'missing hands' shard) by repointing every hand/finger/glove bone per L/R side to that side's wrist bone (bone_L-hand/bone_R-hand) and rebaking offset=meshWorld*inv(wristWorld) so each hand rides its wrist as one rigid body (mirrors the proven RebindInstStringsToRestBasis rigid path). TRADEOFF: fingers no longer articulate (rigid hand) — trades shard for a static-but-coherent hand; the faithful finger-articulating fix is the CharBones pose-pipeline basis (engine, out of lane fence). flag-OFF byte-identical (getenv-cached early return in BandCharacter::NativeRepinHandsRigid) [BandCharacter.cpp]", "RB3_HANDS_POSEAWARE" },
{ "RB3_HANDS_RESKIN", "off", FlagClass::Workaround, FlagRead::Presence, "skinning/hands", "not-live REFUTED, do-NOT default-flip (Wave 14 Lane RESKIN R2): the R1-headline per-member hands reskin. Synthesized per-vertex weighted multi-bone blend (RndMeshDeform::Reskin LBS primitive, computed directly in BandCharacter native code) that re-poses hands_naked verts from the authored bind basis onto the member's OWN gender-posed rest, wired at SyncObjects rest time (post-SetDeformation, authored offsets intact), once-per-mesh-pointer latched, composing with the default-ON RebindHeadHandsAtRest rebake. Fires correctly (all bones resolved, gender-distinct: female 40 bones/1256v vs male 38 bones/1876v, per-member in-place mutate, zero engine TU edits). MEASURED a REGRESSION on the pre-registered IK_SHARD_VERT wext gate (gameplay burst, N~1000 draws/arm): hands_naked wext flag-OFF 60-106u mean 74.8 (39 distinct=animating) -> flag-ON 60-105u mean 87.7 (WORSE); reskin-alone (RB3_NO_HEAD_REBIND) 75-187u mean 136 (much worse). E1 band screenshots corroborate (flag-ON = LARGER hand shards, both genders). ROOT CAUSE (refutes R1's rest-shape thesis): the hands shard is an ANIMATION-BASIS problem (own_rest vs own_live rotation, R*sin(theta) far-vert smear), NOT a rest-shape/bind-basis one; a one-time vertex re-pose leaves the animation delta identical by construction and amplifies the shard (re-posed verts sit at larger radius). Same dead-end class as the refuted RB3_APPENDAGE_REST_ROT / RB3_APPENDAGE_ASSET_REBAKE; the genuine fix is asset/skeleton-basis (skeleton_unshared.milo per-member bind), not any vert/offset bake. Kept in-tree default-OFF as the definitive measured artifact so the per-member-reskin lever is not re-attempted. flag-OFF inert (early-return) / Wii byte-identical (#ifdef HX_NATIVE) [rb3 BandCharacter.cpp NativeReskinHandsAtRest + SyncObjects] | GT-D CLOSURE (Wave 18, execution/R5-HANDS-ENDGAME/CLOSURE.md): hands family CLOSED without articulated ground truth (D5+VISCAP exhausted: nav solved, substrate never animates band CharBones). Accepted residual: hands may articulate wrongly/appear displaced at extreme animated poses, most visible close-up, no mesh tearing (RB3_NO_SKIN_CLAMP is NOT a hands mitigation - rebound-skip). Reopen condition pre-registered in CLOSURE.md; do not re-attempt dead cells.", "RB3_HANDS_RESKIN" },
{ "RB3_HANDS_SHELL_FIX", "off", FlagClass::Workaround, FlagRead::Presence, "skinning", "not-live: W2.8g (Wave 12 Lane B, B-S2) DIAGNOSTIC of the ONE untried SPACE-axis reconciliation cell, default-OFF. B-S1 named the axis SPACE/composition (per-bone rigid conjugation of the finger sub-shell by ~87deg, isoDistort~0 + orthoResid~0, the authored-vertex-to-offset composition). Two prior single-bone cells failed: DEFAULT own-live(magnet 106deg)+own-rest => coherent-at-rest but R*sin(theta) fling SHARD; RB3_APPENDAGE_ASSET_REBAKE bound-live(per-member 129deg)+bound-rest => correct basis but bound is a STATIC copy => FREEZE (5th dead class). This cell = own-live (ANIMATES, no freeze) + bound-rest (per-member 129deg authored basis): bind appendage meshes to the animating magnet bone but bake off=meshWorld*inv(NativeCharSpaceRestXfm(bound)). PREDICTION from the W2.8e pose-INDEPENDENT 87.3deg/68.8deg magnet-vs-per-member gap: at own-rest skin=meshWorld*inv(129deg)*106deg=meshWorld*R_87 => shard-AT-rest, i.e. the 87deg is irreducible with any single live bone (only conjugation W2.8c[dead] or a per-member ANIMATING instance carrying skeleton_unshared.milo authored rest closes it, the latter a loader/skeleton-merge fix OUT of Lane B renderer/composition scope). Settle-guarded (pre-Character::Poll clip-free capture). flag-OFF byte-identical (drawlog 792, getenv-cached, HX_NATIVE) [BandCharacter.cpp RebindHeadHandsAtRest]", "RB3_HANDS_SHELL_FIX" },
