{ "RB3_VENUE_WHITE_GUARD", "off", FlagClass::Workaround, FlagRead::Presence, "render/lighting", "not-live: WHITE-fix (Wave 9/10 STEP-0) scene-side luminance-preserving venue highlight compression. The engaged-venue WHITE over-exposure is baked into the scene render (standard_wgsl.inc per-channel softClipLighting + compressHighlights drive hot pale surfaces to zero-chroma white before the Stage-2 composite samples them), so the Wave-8 chroma-preserve composite fix cannot recover it. ON sets SceneUniforms.venueHighlightLumaMode=1 on the engaged world.cam venue upload -> the standard fragment shader compresses LUMINANCE (not per-channel) and scales RGB uniformly, so a hot venue moment stays bright-but-colored (retail/GX look) instead of clipping white. Identity below the highlight knee; scoped to the venue path (DC3/menus/game.cam leave the field 0 -> per-channel branch, byte-identical). Repurposes the SceneUniforms _padPL[0] pad (size stays 656, static_assert intact); default-OFF, flag-OFF byte-identical (drawlog 792) [Rnd_Wgpu_RB3.cpp + standard_wgsl.inc + UniformStructs.h]", "RB3_VENUE_WHITE_GUARD" },
